[$in title:["Traits"]]
[$in description:["Static trait contracts, explicit conformance and generic bounds in Moth."]]
[$in head:[language_theme_head]]

[navbar]
[sidebar]
listed = sync_navigation(sidebar_id)!
[section, $md:
    # Traits

    A trait names a set of methods. A type declares that it provides those
    methods with `must`. A generic function can then use the trait as a
    @#generic-trait-bounds (bound) and call those methods on its argument.
    Moth checks each concrete argument type at compile time.

    The @#core-cast-traits (core cast traits) use the same mechanism to let
    `cast` convert a struct or choice to a builtin type.
]

